;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jerrylockard.me — DNS zone for Cloudflare
;;
;; Import: Cloudflare dashboard -> jerrylockard.me -> DNS -> Records ->
;;         "Import and Export" -> Import DNS records -> upload this file.
;;
;; AFTER IMPORTING, DO TWO THINGS:
;;
;;   1. Set the apex A record and the www CNAME to DNS only (grey cloud), not
;;      proxied (orange cloud). Vercel has to complete its own TLS challenge on
;;      these names, and Cloudflare's proxy intercepts it. You can turn the
;;      proxy back on later once the certificate is issued, but only with
;;      SSL/TLS mode set to Full (strict) — "Flexible" forces plain HTTP to
;;      Vercel and produces an endless redirect loop.
;;
;;   2. Check the A record value below against Vercel: project -> Settings ->
;;      Domains -> the jerrylockard.me card. 76.76.21.21 is Vercel's
;;      general-purpose apex address, but newer projects are issued a different
;;      one from their anycast pool (216.198.79.1 is another). If the card shows
;;      something else, the card wins — edit the record after import.
;;
;; Deliberately NOT in this file:
;;
;;   MX      Nothing receives mail at @jerrylockard.me. Published contact is
;;           jerry@lockard.tech, a separate domain. Adding an MX record with no
;;           mailbox behind it makes mail bounce in a more confusing way than
;;           having none. Add one only when a real mail provider exists.
;;
;;   CAA     No CAA record is intentional. An absent CAA means any CA may
;;           issue, which is what both Vercel (Let's Encrypt) and Cloudflare
;;           (Google Trust Services) need. A restrictive CAA is a common cause
;;           of stuck certificates.
;;
;; Last reviewed: 2026-08-28
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$TTL 300

;; --- the site, on Vercel -------------------------------------------------
;; Apex must be an A record: a CNAME cannot coexist with other records at the
;; zone root. Cloudflare would flatten one, but the import file has to be valid.
jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	A	76.76.21.21

;; www points at the apex rather than a Vercel hostname, so there is only one
;; Vercel-specific value in this file to keep correct. Add www.jerrylockard.me
;; as a domain in the Vercel project too, or Vercel answers that Host with a
;; 404 — then let Vercel redirect www to the apex.
www.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	CNAME	jerrylockard.me.

;; --- mail: this domain sends and receives nothing ------------------------
;; SPF with -all and no senders: any message claiming to be from
;; @jerrylockard.me fails authentication outright.
jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 -all"

;; DKIM wildcard with an empty key: no selector can ever validate a signature.
*._domainkey.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=DKIM1; p="

;; DMARC set to reject, applied to subdomains as well. No rua= on purpose:
;; sending reports to an address at another domain (lockard.tech) needs an
;; authorisation record published over there first, and a broken rua is worse
;; than none.
_dmarc.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s"
